docs {
  Step 2 of the Reports flow — kicks off asynchronous generation of a report. This returns
  immediately with an `Id`; the report itself is generated in the background.

  **Parameters/Body** (`body:json`)
  - `templateId` — the numeric template ID from "1.Get Report Templates" (e.g. `500` for "Calling
    Detailed Call History").
  - `startDate` / `endDate` — the date range to report on (`YYYY-MM-DD`). Note: 13 months worth of
    reports are available, but each individual report has a 31-day max duration.

  **Usage**: Make a note of the `Id` in the response, and use it to populate `{{reportid}}` for
  "3.Get Report Status".

  See also: https://help.webex.com/en-us/article/nmug598/Reports-for-Your-Cloud-Collaboration-Portfolio

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/reports/create-a-report

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}

